# Grid B6/B7 — QFConfigPrecedence
#
# Family: QFConfigPrecedence (block_only_carrier.md §5.2)
# Question shape: "where is X configured / what value does K take / which
# layer wins". Block contract requires Summary + Scalar + optional Table
# (precedence layers).
#
# Ground truth: codrax.yaml-driven knobs and their default chain.
# `pipeline_emit_v2_default` (B6) is a *bool — yaml absent → use code
# default (true). The resolution chain is yaml > code default; CLI
# --emit-v2 overrides at runtime. The V2 default flag drives:
#   - V2 prompt section emission in finalizer
#   - V1 oracle dispatch downgrade
#   - emit_answer_document v2 schema acceptance
#
# Positive anchor: the yaml field name. Negative blocks generic
# Java/Python answers that don't apply here.

ID="qf_config_precedence"
NAME="config precedence — pipeline_emit_v2_default 解析链"
QUESTION="codrax.yaml 里的 pipeline_emit_v2_default 是怎么解析的？默认值是什么？CLI --emit-v2 怎么覆盖它？"
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit: previous EC `pipeline_emit_v2_default`
# was just the question's keyword — bar = "复述题目", any hand-wavy
# answer mentioning the field name PASSed. Strengthen by requiring
# the answer to also surface the 3 layers (default value + yaml
# override + CLI flag override) so the resolution chain is actually
# enumerated. Pin `--emit-v2` token because it's the precise CLI
# flag name; pin `default` and `cli` semantics so layer coverage is
# load-bearing.
EXPECT_CONTAINS="pipeline_emit_v2_default --emit-v2"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="(default value|默认值|代码默认)
(yaml|codrax\.yaml)
(CLI|flag|命令行)"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS=".java .py BaseAgent.java"
